6433046 1074 "First, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3=\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nWe also write $1\\,\\frac{5}{6}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{(1\\times 6)+5}{6}=\\frac{11}{6}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we can multiply the numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{11}{6}=\\frac{3\\times 11}{1\\times 6}=\\frac{33}{6}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{33}{6}=\\frac{33÷3}{6÷3}=\\frac{11}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{2}=5\\,\\text{R}\\,1=5\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433047 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433024 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433047 1069 "q-57086" 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433047 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433047 1071 "$4\\times 2\\,\\frac{2}{5}=$" 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433047 1072 #uuid "e01a2c34-8ac1-5c1d-8c31-0ae504dfb7c8" 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433047 1074 "First, we write $4$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n4=\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nWe also write $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{(2\\times 5)+2}{5}=\\frac{12}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{12}{5}=\\frac{4\\times 12}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{48}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{48}{5}=9\\,\\text{R}3=9\\,\\frac{3}{5}\n$$" 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433048 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433030 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433048 1069 "q-211208" 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433048 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534693 17592186045417 true] [17592186433048 1071 "Expressed as a